Leading :PROCEDURE blocks do not count as top-level statements, so the
script-level :PARAMETERS after them does not fire diag.parameters_first.
The LSP tolerates this layout; the style guide treats it as wrong
(AGENTS.md section 5), which this scenario pins as current behavior.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Square;
	:PARAMETERS nSide;
	:RETURN nSide * nSide;
:ENDPROC;
:PARAMETERS nInput;
:DECLARE nArea;
nArea := DoProc("Square", {nInput});
:RETURN nArea;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Square;
	:PARAMETERS nSide;
	:RETURN nSide * nSide;
:ENDPROC;
:PARAMETERS nInput;
:DECLARE nArea;
nArea := DoProc("Square", {nInput});
:RETURN nArea;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
